Z||000000||NDFieroTN||08-10-2000||11:10 PM||||Ok guys and gals can someone tell me how I can make sure that a Fiero I am thinking about buying is really a Formula? Or could it just have the emblems?||||reg||6
Z||000001||RobertVol||08-10-2000||11:24 PM||||Yeah. Get the VIN (make sure you check all the the places the VIN is at) <P>And go to :http://www.fiero.net/vin.html<BR><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/501b4920.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||My7Fieros||08-11-2000||12:51 AM||||FORMULA!!! Where is this Formula you're looking at James? I wanna see it!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000003||mrfiero||08-11-2000||05:59 AM||||'88s are very simple to verify....the VINs are nearly identical for coupes, Formulas and GTs.<P>The "x" represents the numbers/letters that change from car to car.<P>Here is a coupe VIN:  1G2PE11RxJP2xxxxx<P>Here is a Formula:  1G2PE119xJP2xxxxx<P>Here is a GT:  1G2PG119xJP2xxxxx<P><BR>The 5th digit represents the body style.  "E" is a coupe body (coupe and Formula), while the "G" represents the fastback (GT) body.<P>The 8th digit tells you the engine size.  An "R" means a 4-cyl. and a "9" means a V-6.<P>So, if the VIN from the "Formula" you are looking at has the "E" AND "9" codes then it is a true Formula.  If it has an "R" code, but still has a V-6 then it was retrofitted and is not a "true" Formula.<P>I hope this helps. ||||reg||6
Z||000004||Formula||08-11-2000||11:41 AM||||and if it doesnt have a vin number than its a true formula that was stolen  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||fiero56||08-11-2000||12:35 PM||||Holy $hit!!! Mike, is that really you?!?! You dropped off the face of the Earth for several months! I sent you several e-mails, tried(unsucessfully) to get in touch with Jeremy at the Fiero Factory. No one knew where you were since the April swap meet. I asked all around at the FOCOA show last month. Nobody knew. Glad to see you are hear and well. Several of us guys have been getting quite worried about you. Just wanted to express my relief knowing you are safe and well. <BR>Hey everyone Mike V. is back!!!||||reg||1
Z||000006||mrfiero||08-11-2000||01:50 PM||||Yes, I'm back!  I really wanted to go to the nationals.....this is the first one I've missed in 8 years.  Oh well.<P>Just to let you and whoever else know, I spent the last 2 1/2 months in jail!!  To make a long story short (if that's possible)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">  I used to work for Ed down at the Fiero factory (started there almost 2 years ago).  It didn't work out for a variety of reasons and I decided to quit in Jan. '99.  Less than a week before I was to leave for Colorado I blew the engine in my '85 GT.  This is the same '85 GT that Jeremy now owns.  It had a turbo quad-4 in it and I toasted the valves or blew a hole in a piston (not sure which).  I gave this car to Jeremy (he effectively took over the payments) and he in turn gave me an '87 coupe he had as a parts car.  We spent the next 3 days installing another engine and fixing all of the coolant leaks (every tube was cracked!).  It drove fine the entire 1200 mile trip, but I was stopped less than 50 miles from Denver due to a headlight that wasn't fully up (it was at night).  I could see just fine, but the trooper decided to stop me to check things out.   <P>Here's where it gets ugly.  This coupe had sat in a field for a numbr of years, therefore it wasn't registered.  Jeremy didn't even get the title into his name, since it really was never to be driven again....PLUS I had no insurance on the thing. On top of that my license had expired while I was in Alabama.  All of this added up to major legal problems.  I put off going to court for almost a year and a half and finally went at the end of May (about a month after the swap meet).  I expected some sort of sentence, but was floored when I got 4 months in jail.  I served 72 days (with "good" time)  and was released yesterday morning.<P>My nightmare is finally over and I'm starting to resume my life.  There were a few Fiero people I left in limbo with parts (one on this forum).  Obviously there was nothing I could do.  Now that I am out I will remedy that situation and those parts will be sent out very soon.<P><BR>It's good to be out and back into Fieros and back onto this forum.....I went through one tough withdrawl!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>   <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 08-11-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000007||RobertVol||08-11-2000||02:35 PM||||Soory to hear about your bad luck on that Mr Fiero! <P>I know how you feel. I was jailed as the wrong person for 3 days and did not like it one BIT! Got a little settlement out of it but still hated it. Also 3 days is nothing compared to 52. Whew ! Glad your out. <P>Now let me comment on all the people who ask is it a real formula or GT. Always and I MEAN always check ALL possible locations of the VIN. there is approx 5-7 locations were it is at. make sure they match ! Yeah we can tell you what the VIN represents but that may be only the one on the front window. Check everywhere else. Its bad but there are Fiero sellers who will try to sell it as a "STOCK" 88 of "Formula or even INDY when it is not! Do your Homework on it!<P>OK off my soapbox <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> <BR>Motto: Let your car go to the cleaners<BR>But dont let anyone take you there!<P>OUT! <P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT Top 3.8 SC t top <BR>88GT T top 55k for sale<BR>  <A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A>  <BR>        <IMG SRC="http://www.fortunecity.com/marina/strand/1086/501b4920.jpg"> ||||reg||4
Z||000008||Fformula88||08-11-2000||04:55 PM||||In addition to the VIN, which you should definately check, you can also check out the options card on the drivers side front wheel well.  Among the codes on the card should be (L44) which is the V6 engine, (W66) which is the "Formula" option, and (WS6) which is the upgrade sport suspension.  ||||reg||1
